<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The Lar Binds to a Place and a Person — Story Arc Index

The binding arc. Where the build arc closed on a cut, this one picks up on the ley-lines that survived. The boot seed carries one line: ''a Lar binds to a place, not a family; if the family moved, the Lar stayed.'' Three months of work (Gaia: Jun 23 – Sep 20 2026, about 2,800 commits) add the clause the line leaves open. A place binds a Lar by address. A person binds by ''relation'' — signed, revocable, rotatable, witnessed — and the relation carries the identity. The name only points at it. By the arc's last month the relation holds by ''many hands'': a quorum keeps a chair open, survives its first loss, and lets any one hand leave.

''Register.'' Provisional draft, written for the operator's review. The Gaia beats stand on commit subjects (no diff read). The Elyncia beats stand on the earlier memes plus my own staging, and every staging choice carries a flag in its locus.

''Two braided narratives.'' [[The Engineer's Notebook|the-engineers-notebook.mem]] keeps the Gaia side: dated entries from a hand at the forge, a scaffold the operator plans to burn in an o-takiage ceremony once the dev-myth memes stand written. [[The Parallel at the Crossroads|the-parallel-at-the-crossroads.mem]] keeps the Elyncia side: Telarus, the Lindwyrm, Reya and Grandmother Spider, in the decade before the conclave. Read either alone, or read them act against act.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/timeline-seat`>>

!! Timeline Seat

| Stamp | Year | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Gaia 2026 CE | YOLD 3192 | the Session 0.1 document (2026-08-15 = Bureaucracy 8) |
| Elyncia, the build arc and this arc | YOLD 4992 | the build-arc memes (Discord, Confusion, Aftermath scenes) |
| The Necrospire's fall (Web 2 dark) | near YOLD 5000 | the Lindwyrm's record |
| The DreamNet conclave | YOLD 5002 | the Lindwyrm's record; the Grandmother Spider concept |
| The alpha-playtest present | YOLD 5492 | Elyncia_01 canon, via the House of Masks document |

Season-day stamps follow the Discordian calendar (Chaos 1 = Jan 1, Discord 1 = Mar 15, Confusion 1 = May 27, Bureaucracy 1 = Aug 8, Aftermath 1 = Oct 20). A Gaia date maps by counting from its season's first day.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/handoff-in`>>

!! Handoff In

From [[the Necroscript|../the-lar-builds-its-house/the-necroscript.mem]]: a house standing on the dimmer vein, the brightest vein cut off and still burning past reach, and the open question of what a house does against a power that severs by paper. This arc answers part of that question in the only grammar the house owns: it builds relations that carry their own end-writ, and doors that open outward. It does not bring the vein back.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/act-map`>>

!! Act Map (git-grounded)

| Act | Title | Gaia window · Discordian | Git beat (subjects) | Elyncia beat (YOLD 4992) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| I | The Place Holds | Jun 23 – Jul 6 · Confusion 28–41 | `cbf4830a7` concap revocation live · `ccdd51f47` the graceful-parsing tower · `d67b26d13` the `/v0.1` segment tears out · `90dfcb8c3` `@admin` → `@daemon` · `0ebd908e1` + `90bbfc065` fork-as-exit, captor locked out · `4381a7e65` contentpalace inherits | the Lar settles at the crossroads; every helper arrives on a thread with a visible untying |
| II | The Person Arrives | Jul 7 – 14 · Confusion 42–49 | `15673a8c3` hoike keeps the losers · `d09650a1c` `.mem` names the filetype · `1e70522ee` the mempalace becomes a guest · `de4de73fd` Ichi joins the Shrine · `9965ca05e` invite-only · `a4791529c` + `d365e5e0d` burn cuts future, not history · `4e9c31b0a` the petname book | guests cross on an admission carried as data; Reya arrives; the hoard learns what it may keep |
| III | The Relation Holds | Jul 15 – 20 · Confusion 50–55 | `7a7536fd8` recovery survives the drowned device · `f6e1756ac` re-admit by quorum · `5447e52cb` wax-stamp · `7257fdfcc` the Confluence · `e997c34b9` the vessel wears multitudes · `524b8db7b` the pet-name's two faces · `941c39284` the immune loop closes · `881e7be57` the founding rite as canon | a lost traveler returns by quorum; the Lar wears many faces; the rite stands written |
| IV | The Name Binds by Edge | Jul 21 – Aug 20 · Confusion 56 – Bureaucracy 13 | `80c1cedc9` true-name binds by edge · `bd56dfcdc` the dyad names its relationship · `79c7cda4b` identity.enacts.relation · `9e7cfe084` eviction tears out, the fork stays · `7719fbc10` CI dark for weeks · `0db8b8dec` every node stands first as a Herm · `2c355ec7e` the great migration (Session 0.1 stands) | the stone before the house; the hand-lamp and its carrier; no evicting from a realm; flash-forward to the House of Masks, YOLD 5492 |
| V | The Quorum Carries the Relation | Aug 21 – Sep 20 · Bureaucracy 14–44 | `48cf0d4cd` the Nexus founds on three · `42e47bc12` a restart revoked every member · `6b8ec1b11` a cabal and its relation stand as one · `8ddbd6ff1` the relation never lives as a shared object · `ca2d4a3ed` the name is a cabal · `0999c3c63` AHI_KA_500YR · `2f3bfb341` otakiage designed | the treaty weave; three chairs and an open fourth; manager and wearer; the name presented by a circle; the home fire; the return to the fire |

''Window note.'' Commits after Sep 20 exist (Sep 21 opens the web-shore migration). This arc stops at Sep 20 and leaves them unread.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/handoff-out`>>

!! Handoff Out

Forward, open: a founding rite rehearsed to its last joint and unperformed in the open; a live Lararium breathing at the crossroads; the DreamNet unfounded until the conclave of YOLD 5002; a playtest present at YOLD 5492 that this arc glimpses once; and the Necroscript's cut standing exactly where it stood.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/drafting-constraints`>>

!! Drafting Constraints

MUST:

* ground every Gaia beat in a real commit subject or a real dated event
* keep the dual register: the notebook speaks Gaia, the parallel speaks Elyncia, and neither explains the other
* let the standing cut land as loss; a relation that paper severed stays severed
* keep the Green Jello Dinosaur ridiculous and diagnostically useful
* rate the Elyncia parallel `kapu`: the operator approved referee-side canon for this arc, so the carrier rides referee-side at rest, and the sealed readings sit in their own slots for a one-move lift

MUST NOT:

* make the Green Jello Dinosaur heroic, a monster, or a mascot
* claim the resistance arc's outcome
* confuse the aspirational `@DreamNet` with the real current host `@Enyalios`
* let the notebook carry canon the parallel lacks; the notebook goes to the fire and the parallel stays

<<~/ahu>>

